    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-11-07T18:21:53+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-07T18:21:53+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:51:53Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:51:53Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred well south of SA will continue to drift eastwards over the weekend, while a developing low pressure system and trough in WA move close to the SA border. The high drifts southeast of Tasmania by Monday as the low moves across western SA on Monday and northern SA on Tuesday before clearing to the east later. Another high develops south of the bight on Wednesday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-11-07T18:19:21+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T07:49:21Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, most likely in the evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm west of Coober Pedy. Thunderstorms possibly severe with damaging winds north of Marla. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 40 km/h.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-11-08T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-07T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. The chance of a thunderstorm, possibly severe with damaging winds north of Marla. Winds east to southeasterly 25 to 35 km/h tending east to northeasterly 35 to 50 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 24 with daytime temperatures reaching 30 to 40.</text>
                <text type="fire_danger">High</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 9:10am to 5:10pm, UV Index predicted to reach 11 [Extreme]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-11-09T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-08T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Medium chance of showers south of Woomera, slight chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm. The chance of raised dust south of Coober Pedy in the late morning and afternoon. Winds northeasterly 30 to 45 km/h tending northwest to southwesterly in the middle of the day then tending southeast to southwesterly 25 to 40 km/h in the late afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 16 and 23 with daytime temperatures reaching 34 to 39.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-11-10T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-09T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Slight chance of a shower west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm with little or no rainfall. Winds southeast to southwesterly 25 to 35 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 13 and 19 with daytime temperatures reaching 26 to 33.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-11-11T00:00:00+10:30" end-time-local="2026-11-12T00:00:00+10:30" start-time-utc="2026-11-10T13:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-11-11T13:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Mostly sunny. Slight chance of a shower north of Marla, most likely in the afternoon and evening. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Coober Pedy. Winds south to southeasterly 20 to 30 km/h. Overnight temperatures falling to between 11 and 17 with daytime temperatures reaching around 30.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
